[Music]  we once again return to part four of the  heroes path  a seven-part mini-series covering the  various journeys of the most important  characters  while embroiled in the chaos that was  the great calamity  if you haven't already be sure to check  out the previous parts and especially  the one about link and zelda  since the later episodes skip over most  of the introduction established in that  one  and start right away at the moment of  ganon's rise  joining me today all the way from the  fifth dimension  the master of hype mr hmk  i am very excited to finally have him on  the channel  be sure to check out his amazing  theories as well as his podcast the  fifth dimension  in which he invites various guests to  talk about specific games  one of which recently hosted a plethora  of zelda theorists including me to sit  down and talk  about the upcoming hyrule warriors age  of calamity  and let me tell you the hype is real  and now it is time to get this show on  the road  once again  as the ground begins to shake beneath  the feet of the champions and the  princess and the sky begins to glow in  ominous red color ravali takes flight  to investigate the commotion to his  shock he sees the center point  of the hilaine civilization being  enveloped in a whirlpool of dark clouds  lightning and a ghostly specter soaring  above the peaks  of the majestic hyrule castle he reports  his findings to the rest of the group  and after discussing a strategy he and  the rest of the party  take to the road or in rivalli's case  the skies  blessed with the advantage of wounded  flight ravali soars upwards to start his  journey  towards valmetto located in rito village  within the hebrew province in terms of  distance his divine beast is  actually the furthest from the promenade  however without the hurdles of having to  scale mountains and stick to the roads  his path leading to his ancient machine  is by far the easiest  unless he had some company along the way  something we'll get into shortly  now we don't know exactly how fast  rivali is  but it's safe to say that with his  advantage of being able to fly  he will likely be one of the first if  not the first to reach his divine beast  with mifa being a possible contender  since varuta is by far the closest to  the promenade  with such a straightforward path you  would expect rivali's journey to be the  most boring and unnecessary one to  depict through gameplay  and there is a possibility that his road  to valmero  will simply not be included as a  gameplay section  but let's spice it up a bit and sketch  some awesome  yet very speculative scenarios age of  calamity could potentially use  to make rivals journey more interesting  starting with  aerial battles although ravali's path is  depicted as a straightforward one in  creating a champion  one thing that catches the attention is  the fact that he actually flies right  past hyrule castle and even slightly  over the west side of castletown  so what if ravali's weight of our meadow  is hindered by flying enemies  the first of which would come to mind of  course being the guardian skywatcher  the flying battleship variant of the  grounded guardian stalker  this way a path that looks like this  would suddenly transform into something  like this  if the engine of hyrule warriors permits  it aerial combat would definitely spice  up the gameplay  it could make rivalli's missions the  most unique out of all the champions and  would complement his overall skill set  as a master of the bow  we did see a very short clip of rivali  engaging grounded enemies  but in my opinion a weapon like the bow  doesn't reach the same potential as  melee weapons or magic while grounded  since you would have to deal with draw  speed precise aiming and a limited  attack radius  so unless rivali all of a sudden uses  melee attacks as well  something we haven't seen him do at any  point in any of the cutscenes and as far  as we know isn't part of his skill set  there needs to be a different way of  making his combat more interesting hence  fights with flying enemies  there is one possible inconsistency  though and that is that it's not exactly  clear if the guardian skywatchers will  already be present at the castle at the  time ravali is in its vicinity  according to the backstory of breath of  the wild the sky watchers were not part  of the mechanical army the hylians dug  up right before the calamity  as zelda hypothesizes in her research  notes that there are potentially more  guardian  types stored inside the five columns  hidden underneath hyrule castle  if that is indeed where the sky watches  are stored the columns would have to  have risen up by the time rivali reaches  castle town  something we aren't sure of as of right  now and it's still up for debate  whatever the case may be age of calamity  might have to change this part of the  lore to make this work  something i am totally fine with if it  makes for more interesting gameplay  alternatively rivali could come under  attack by other types of flying or  floating enemies  like swarms of keys cursed enemies sky  octorocks or  maybe even wiz ropes could reach these  heights i mean they do float after all  after possibly having fought his way  past central hyrule from up high  revali enters the hebrew region there  are two significant sentiments which  could be used as the stage  for a grounded gameplay section for  rivali that being tabitha village  and his hometown retail village if  aerial combat is not going to be a thing  we might see revali  visit one or both of these settlements  to help fend off  a possible invasion the guardian  stalkers  will in all likelihood not play a role  in this  due to its secluded location tabantha  village wasn't attacked by the guardians  until later stages of the calamity and  rito village  was spared this fate all together by the  time the guardians were getting close to  the home of the rito  zelda sealed calamity ganon after which  he lost  most direct control of his mechanical  army  so in this case these invasions or  attacks would have to be related to  monsters  ravali isn't exactly the most selfless  character  but even if he doesn't care much for the  fate of tabitha village he would  at the very least not leave his own  people to fend off for themselves  if retail village is under monster  attack he would in all probability  join the battle to ensure the safety of  his tribe and then move on to his divine  beast as soon as things are under  control  vamero is located pretty much at retail  village  so from there it's a straight shot to  its final destination  with that said the next scenario is one  we haven't discussed so far in the  series  and was purposely saved for this episode  if all previous scenarios  don't come to fruition there is yet  another way  to really make rival's journey very  interesting  since what if we actually get to control  the meadow for a while what other divine  beasts  this is a bit harder to imagine since  they would have to interact with the  complex geography of hyrule  like mountains rivers and valleys since  valmetto is airborne  this really isn't too much of a stretch  on top of that  rivali's war machine isn't just armed  with a giant laser which will probably  just be overkill against smaller enemies  but it's also equipped with bow cannons  perhaps  we could switch between these different  cannons and blast incoming enemies out  of the sky  by this point the giant pillars  surrounding hyrule castle  most definitely would have risen so sky  watchers are now  guaranteed to be flying around as soon  as ravali gets vamedo into position to  take aim at calamity ganon himself  the demon king uses his malice to  corrupt the divine beast  turning it from friend to foe ravali is  faced with one of ganon's horrific  phantoms which has now deemed itself the  new master of the ancient machine  a fight ensues between dorito warrior  and wind blight ganon  a fight which determines the fate of the  many inhabitants of hyrule since the  destructive power of valmeado  would be any settlement's worst  nightmare after a fierce battle  rivali is eventually bested by his  opponent and falls to the hands of the  merciless phantom  he suffers the same fate as the other  champions with his spirit now trapped  inside the technological prowess  he worked so hard for to master but all  was not  for nothing despite losing the fight and  thus his life to win blight canon he  managed to keep up the fight long enough  so that valmetto was never to be used  against his allies  with the power to vaporize entire cities  with ease it would have been  unimaginable what could have happened  had rivali not been there to hold of his  nemesis for as long as he did  with the shortest lifespan of all of  hyrule's races  no rito present at the time of breath of  the wild was alive at the time of  rivali's passing  however his memory is passed on among  his tribe  and their children are raised to be  brave and skilled like their legendary  ancestor  as for rivali himself he will eventually  get his sweet revenge  due to the efforts of what was once his  biggest rival from 100 years ago  [Music]  you

